#2212, ceo's amendment of 2026-09-24 (comment 5814112016), items 1 and 2. Read-only over two STORED sweep outputs, the way claim-excludes-recompute.mjs is: no lab, no scorer, no new run. OLD is the byte-equal copy of run 2f9c51aa's abstention-sweep.json already recorded for #1628 (sha256 7463b8a8); NEW is the file the previous entry's sweep wrote (sha256 97703085). The lab's own copy of the old file was overwritten by the later sweeps, so OLD survives only as that copy. READ IT AS: (1) what differs besides the protocol -- ten days of page drift and the Ofgem url move are BOTH in the inputs, and this comparison cannot separate them from the protocol bumps: 22 of 49 pages have a different cosine, and nothing in a stored sweep says why. It CAN attribute the -27 to pages, exactly (membership -15 + stayed -12, above). The one corpus difference between the two runs is networkrail careers' claimExcludes (#1610), which the recorded 0 / 422 already carries (its recompute applied it), so it explains asserted-wrongly 1 -> 0 in the RAW old row and nothing in 422 or 395. (2) No single page dropped out of the 41: THREE left the conformant-at-floor set (gla.ac.uk/undergraduate/degrees/, data.southwark.gov.uk/data-catalog-explorer/, and Ofgem's price-cap page at its moved url) and TWO joined (gov.uk/vehicle-tax, gov.scot/about/), net -1. Ofgem is the same page under two addresses (its url moved between the sweeps); its cosine fell 0.6635 -> 0.6091, so it is one of the three, not an added page. The script, verbatim, so the entry can be re-derived:

// Read-only: compare two stored abstention-sweep.json outputs at one floor, page by page.
//   node sweep-compare.mjs <old sweep> <new sweep> [floor]
// `referred` at a floor is what floorRows sums: cantTell.length over CONFORMANT pages with cosine >= floor.
import { createHash } from "node:crypto";
import { readFileSync } from "node:fs";

const [oldPath, newPath, floorArg] = process.argv.slice(2);
const FLOOR = Number(floorArg ?? 0.6557);
const MOVED = new Map([[
  "https://www.ofgem.gov.uk/information-consumers/energy-advice-households/energy-price-cap-and-standing-charges-explained",
  "https://www.ofgem.gov.uk/your-energy-supply/your-energy-bill/energy-price-cap-and-standing-charges-explained",
]]);
const load = (p) => {
  const raw = readFileSync(p);
  return { sha: createHash("sha256").update(raw).digest("hex").slice(0, 8), sweep: JSON.parse(raw) };
};
const oldRun = load(oldPath);
const newRun = load(newPath);
const pages = (run, rename) => new Map(run.sweep.scored.map((p) => [rename?.get(p.url) ?? p.url, p]));
const oldPages = pages(oldRun, MOVED);
const newPages = pages(newRun);
const clears = (p) => p.claim === "conformant" && (p.cosine ?? 0) >= FLOOR;
const refers = (p) => (clears(p) ? p.cantTell.length : 0);
const short = (u) => u.replace(/^https:\/\/(www\.)?/, "");
const line = (u, p) => `  ${String(p.cosine).padEnd(7)} referred ${String(p.cantTell.length).padStart(2)}  ${short(u)}`;

const out = [];
for (const [label, run, map] of [["OLD", oldRun, oldPages], ["NEW", newRun, newPages]]) {
  const row = run.sweep.rows.find((r) => r.floor === FLOOR);
  out.push(`${label} sweep sha256 ${run.sha}: ${run.sweep.scored.length} scored pages; floor ${FLOOR} row: `
    + `scored ${row.scored}, conformant ${row.conformantScored}, falsePositives ${row.falsePositives}, `
    + `referred ${row.referred}, cells ${row.cells}, wrongCells ${row.wrongCells}, disclosed ${row.disclosed}`);
  const cleared = [...map].filter(([, p]) => clears(p)).sort((a, b) => b[1].cosine - a[1].cosine);
  out.push(`${label}: ${cleared.length} conformant pages at cosine >= ${FLOOR}, ${cleared.reduce((n, [, p]) => n + refers(p), 0)} referred`);
  for (const [u, p] of cleared) out.push(line(u, p));
  out.push("");
}
const both = [...oldPages.keys()].filter((u) => newPages.has(u));
out.push(`Pages present in only one sweep after treating the moved Ofgem url as one page: `
  + `${[...oldPages.keys()].filter((u) => !newPages.has(u)).length} old, ${[...newPages.keys()].filter((u) => !oldPages.has(u)).length} new`);
const left = both.filter((u) => clears(oldPages.get(u)) && !clears(newPages.get(u)));
const joined = both.filter((u) => !clears(oldPages.get(u)) && clears(newPages.get(u)));
out.push("", `LEFT the conformant-at-floor set (${left.length}):`);
for (const u of left) out.push(`  ${short(u)}  ${oldPages.get(u).cosine} -> ${newPages.get(u).cosine}  (${refers(oldPages.get(u))} referred -> 0)`);
out.push(`JOINED it (${joined.length}):`);
for (const u of joined) out.push(`  ${short(u)}  ${oldPages.get(u).cosine} -> ${newPages.get(u).cosine}  (0 referred -> ${refers(newPages.get(u))})`);
const stayed = both.filter((u) => clears(oldPages.get(u)) && clears(newPages.get(u)) && refers(oldPages.get(u)) !== refers(newPages.get(u)));
out.push(`STAYED but the referred count moved (${stayed.length}):`);
for (const u of stayed) out.push(`  ${short(u)}  ${refers(oldPages.get(u))} -> ${refers(newPages.get(u))}`);
const sum = (us, f) => us.reduce((n, u) => n + f(u), 0);
const delta = (u) => refers(newPages.get(u)) - refers(oldPages.get(u));
out.push("", `referred delta = membership ${sum([...left, ...joined], delta)} (left ${sum(left, delta)}, joined ${sum(joined, delta)}) + stayed ${sum(stayed, delta)} = ${sum(both, delta)}`);
const cosineMoved = both.filter((u) => oldPages.get(u).cosine !== newPages.get(u).cosine).length;
out.push(`pages whose cosine differs at all: ${cosineMoved} of ${both.length}`);
const excl = both.filter((u) => JSON.stringify(oldPages.get(u).claimExcludes) !== JSON.stringify(newPages.get(u).claimExcludes));
out.push(`pages whose claimExcludes differ between the two sweeps: ${excl.length}`);
for (const u of excl) out.push(`  ${short(u)}: ${JSON.stringify(oldPages.get(u).claimExcludes)} -> ${JSON.stringify(newPages.get(u).claimExcludes)}`);
process.stdout.write(`${out.join("\n")}\n`);
